// Title: User Added To Highly Privileged Group
// Sigma ID: 10fb649c-3600-4d37-b1e6-56ea90bb7e09
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-02-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1098
// Description: Detects addition of users to highly privileged groups via "Net" or "Add-LocalGroupMember".
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity that must be investigated
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/slashandgrab-screen-connect-post-exploitation-in-the-wild-cve-2024-1709-cve-2024-1708
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_add_user_privileged_group.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((ProcessCommandLine contains "localgroup " and ProcessCommandLine contains " /add") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "Add-LocalGroupMember " and ProcessCommandLine contains " -Group ")) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Group Policy Creator Owners" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Schema Admins")
